Just to keep things consistant, shouldn't throwing a potion of acid at a
water elemental (and possibly water nymphs and water trolls as well) result
in a little extra damage or maybe even a weak explosion?

Also, this has probably been pointed out before, but nethack has things
backwards when it comes to mixing acid and water. Conventional wisdom is
that if you have to mix concentrated acid and water, always add acid to
water, not the other way around. But in nethack, it's only dipping acid into
water that results in an explosion. Of course, the reaction is exothermic
either way, but that's always seemed "off" to me.

Along those same lines, maybe throwing potions of water at acid blobs ought
to do more than get them wet.



